@startuml gestures
' ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
' ║  THIS FILE IS THE PROGRAM.                                               ║
' ║  Sources/WalkieTalkie/GestureDiagram.swift parses it at launch and       ║
' ║  Sources/WalkieTalkie/GestureMachine.swift executes it. Nothing in       ║
' ║  Sources/ decides what a mouse gesture means — this file does.           ║
' ║  Render with ./docs/build-gestures.sh; never hand-edit docs/gestures.svg.║
' ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
'
' GRAMMAR (the parser accepts exactly this; everything else is decoration):
'
'   [*] --> S                     the initial state, exactly one
'   state S <<stereo>> { … }      one level of nesting; deeper is a parse error
'   S : chip "…"                  one chip row, in file order. THE tooltip.
'   S : entry / a, b              actions run on entering S
'   S : exit  / a                 actions run on leaving S
'   S : 🔼 trigger [g] / a        an INTERNAL transition: no exit, no entry
'   A --> B : 🔼 trigger [g] / a  trigger [guard] / actions
'
'   · The trigger is the LAST whitespace-separated token. The 🔼 / 🔽 / arrow
'     in front is a glyph for the reader and is checked against HotkeyTap's
'     own table by evals/test_gesture_glyphs.py.
'   · A bare trigger must exist in HotkeyTap.triggerNames. An @name is an
'     event the app fires (the world answering, not his hand).
'   · `A --> A` is a PARSE ERROR. A UML self-transition re-runs exit and entry,
'     which here would resume the music and drop the ring for a gesture that is
'     supposed to change nothing. Write an internal transition instead.
'   · Guards and actions are NAMES, never expressions. `!` is the only operator.
'   · Two transitions on the same (state, trigger) are tried in file order,
'     first passing guard wins; at most one unguarded, and it must be last.
'
' THE VOCABULARY, in Victor's words (2026-09-14):
'   "la apăsarea forward simplă începe dictarea, dar apoi dictarea aceea se
'    poate duce în diverse locuri, în funcție de cum se termină gestul"
'   — so the gesture that ENDS the sentence is the one that names where it goes.

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<rest>>    #F6F6F4
  BackgroundColor<<mic>>     #FFF3E2
  BackgroundColor<<waiting>> #ECF2FF
  BorderColor #4A4A4A
  FontName Helvetica
}
title The mouse vocabulary — walkie-talkie

[*] --> Idle

' ── At rest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
state Idle <<rest>>
Idle : chip ""
' 🔼 ↓ — the left button held, then the forward click. **No toggle**, exactly as
' the left-plus-wheel chord it replaces: the gesture is made while pointing at the
' terminal he means, and making it twice means "again", never "let go".
'
' 🔽 ↓ is the same call the menu's **Disconnect** row makes, so the gesture cannot
' end up meaning something subtly other than the row that documents it — including
' the chip's burst, which is the only thing on screen that says it happened.
Idle : 🔼 forward-bind / bindFrontmost
Idle : 🔽 back-down / unbind
Idle : 🔽 back-click / postReturn
Idle : 🔽 back-right / postWisprHandsFree
Idle : @bindArrived / showBinding
Idle : @unbound / showUnbound

' The aim is set BEFORE the microphone is asked for, and again by whichever
' gesture ends the sentence. It has to be first in the list: `openDictation`
' reaches the source, and the local recogniser can raise `didBegin`
' synchronously inside that call.
'
' Where a fresh dictation points is *what a plain ending would do*: at the
' terminal when there is one, at the caret when there is not. 🔼 click says
' caret outright whatever is bound, which is the vocabulary Victor fixed on
' 2026-09-12 and this change does not touch.
'
' **The bind grace is gone from the click**, and stays gone. For three days a
' click made within five seconds of a bind went to the terminal instead, on the
' argument that a bind is him naming a precise destination and the caret is the
' vaguest one. Victor's vocabulary, restated 2026-09-12: *"butonul forward
' pornește dictare la caret (indiferent dacă e legat ceva); forward + right move:
' dictare legată"*. The two gestures are the two destinations, and a click that
' sometimes means the other one is a click he cannot trust.
Idle --> AtCaret  : 🔼 forward-click / aimAtCaret, openDictation
Idle --> ToBound  : 🔼 forward-right [bound] / aimAtBound, openDictation
Idle --> AtCaret  : 🔼 forward-right / aimAtCaret, openDictation
Idle --> ToBound  : ⌨ key-dictate [bound] / aimAtBound, openDictation
Idle --> AtCaret  : ⌨ key-dictate / aimAtCaret, openDictation
' 🔼 ↑ — **dictate at a session that does not exist yet.** A gesture of its own,
' where from 2026-09-05 it was the wheel clicked twice converting a dictation
' already in flight: the wheel had one press to spend and no working hold, so the
' second click was the only spare gesture on it. This button has four directions,
' so the spawn gets one outright and needs nothing to reinterpret. The wheel's
' double click still says this same word (`HotkeyTap.fire`), and at rest it
' therefore *opens* a dictation that is a spawn from its first sample rather than
' converting one.
'
' The context shot is taken at the press, like every other dictation's.
' `deferContext` went with the wheel: it existed because the wheel's *release* was
' the moment the picture wanted — the screen his finger had left, before a second
' click could land — and a gesture that ends with the mouse already moved has no
' such moment. What survives of it is `HotkeyTap.onWheelRelease`, which is a cue
' about *when* to take the frame and deliberately not a gesture.
Idle --> ToSpawn  : 🔼 forward-up / aimAtSpawn, openDictation

' ── The microphone is open ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Everything that is true for the whole sentence, whatever it is aimed at,
' is declared once here rather than re-derived per destination.
state Listening <<mic>> {
  ' The music pause is a genuine EDGE — MusicBridge is told once when the
  ' microphone opens and once when it shuts. The ring, the borrowed gestures
  ' and the chip are NOT actions: they are functions of the state, re-derived
  ' by one reconciler after every transition, which is why they are not on any
  ' arrow. An effect that is a function of the state and an effect that fires
  ' at an instant are two different things and this file distinguishes them.
  Listening : entry / pauseMusic
  Listening : exit  / resumeMusic
  Listening : 🔽 back-click / captureScreenshot
  Listening : 🔽 back-right / postWisprHandsFree
  Listening : @micOpened / confirmMicOpen
  Listening : @micConfirmedShut / noteShut

  ' Where a plain ending would send it. The substate IS the chip.
  state AtCaret
  AtCaret : chip "⌨️ at the caret"
  ' 🔼 ↓ — the left button held 0.3 s, then the forward click. HotkeyTap
  ' judges the chord and fires `forward-bind`; a bare click is `forward-click`.
  ' Victor: "dacă pe drum fac gestul de forward în jos, asta leagă dictarea
  ' de terminalul de sub mouse."
  ' 🔼 → with NOTHING bound does not end the sentence. It refuses, it warns,
  ' and the microphone stays open until he says where the words go. Victor:
  ' "dictarea nu se termină, ci așteaptă să se înțeleagă unde se trimite.
  '  De aia apare warning. Nu la început."  — an INTERNAL transition, so
  ' Listening's exit does not run: music still paused, ring still up.

  state ToBound
  ToBound : chip "🎙️ {boundFolder}"

  state ToSpawn
  ToSpawn : chip "✨ {spawnFolder}"
  ToSpawn : @spawnFolderChosen / nameSpawnFolder

  AtCaret --> ToBound : 🔼 forward-bind / bindFrontmost
  AtCaret --> ToBound : @bindArrived / aimAtBound
  ToSpawn --> ToBound : 🔼 forward-bind / bindFrontmost
  ToBound --> AtCaret : @unbound / aimAtCaret
}

' ── How a sentence ends ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The gesture that ENDS the sentence names where it goes — whatever it was
' aimed at while he was talking. Victor: "dictarea aceea se poate duce în
' diverse locuri, în funcție de cum se termină gestul."
'
' These leave the COMPOSITE, so they apply from all three destinations. A
' substate's own transition outranks its parent's (plain UML), which is how
' AtCaret's refusal below gets first refusal on 🔼 →.
Listening --> Settling : 🔼 forward-click / aimAtCaret, stopDictation
Listening --> Settling : 🔼 forward-right [bound] / aimAtBound, stopDictation
' Mid-sentence, 🔼 ↑ **converts the dictation to a spawn**: same recording, same
' words — only the destination changes. The terminal it opens in does not exist
' yet, so the folder menu is offered exactly as it is at a fresh spawn press.
Listening --> Settling : 🔼 forward-up / aimAtSpawn, stopDictation
Listening --> Settling : ⌨ key-dictate / aimWhereAimed, stopDictation
' ⬅️ — the forward button held and the mouse flicked left (and the wheel held,
' with Logi gestures off). Since 2026-09-12 it throws a **Wispr Flow** dictation
' away too, through the same one call the ✕ and the menu row make. Victor's ask:
' the gesture that abandons a sentence must not depend on which app happens to be
' hearing it.
Listening --> Idle     : 🔼 forward-left / cancelDictation
Listening --> Idle     : @sourceGaveUp / warnSourceSilent

' 🔼 → with NOTHING bound does not end the sentence. Written HERE, after the
' guarded arrow above, because reading order is evaluation order: the guarded
' one gets first refusal and this unguarded one answers when it declines. The
' parser enforces that ordering — writing this line inside the state block
' above shadowed the delivery, and it said so.
'
' Being INTERNAL, Listening's exit does not run: the music stays paused, the
' ring stays up, the microphone stays open. Victor: "dictarea nu se termină, ci
' așteaptă să se înțeleagă unde se trimite. De aia apare warning. Nu la început."
Listening : 🔼 forward-right / warnNothingBound

' ── The words are in flight ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A click here is a stop or nothing, never a new dictation — 2026-09-13's
' phantom dictation, made structurally impossible by there being no arrow.
'
' What it cost the first time, in one line of the imperative code this replaces:
' the first click stopped the microphone; the closing edge came three seconds
' late; a second click landed inside the settle, where the branch asked only about
' `listening`, and started a **phantom dictation** whose `gestureSeen` disarmed
' the first sentence's swallow window. Wispr's ⌘V arrived a second later and
' landed in the Terminal that happened to be in front, and the chip spent twelve
' seconds on a dictation that did not exist. A click while the words are in flight
' is him ending a sentence he has already ended: it is a stop, or it is nothing.
state Settling <<waiting>>
Settling : chip "⏳ Transcribing..."
Settling : 🔼 forward-click / sayInFlight
Settling : 🔼 forward-right / sayInFlight
Settling : 🔼 forward-up / sayInFlight
Settling : 🔽 back-click / captureScreenshot
Settling : @bindArrived / reaim

' **The machine does not deliver.** Where a sentence goes once the words are
' back is `AppDelegate.deliver` → `commit`, a four-way fork over a dead tty, a
' blind-paste target and a spawn that failed to open — delivery routing, not
' gesture semantics, and none of it is decided by the mouse. So `commit` says
' which way it went and the machine follows. Firing `deliver` from here as well
' would send the sentence twice.
Settling --> Idle        : @delivered
Settling --> HeldForBind : @held
Settling --> Idle        : @settleGaveUp / sayNoWords
Settling --> Idle        : 🔼 forward-left / cancelDictation

' ── Nothing was bound when the words landed ────────────────────────────────
' The five-minute hold (holdsForBind, 2026-09-11). Reachable only through
' @held — never through a gesture, because 🔼 → refuses above rather than
' ending a sentence with nowhere to go.
state HeldForBind <<waiting>>
HeldForBind : chip "⏳ bind to send — ⌘⌃B"
HeldForBind : 🔼 forward-bind / bindFrontmost

' `releaseAwaitingBind` is reached from `showBound`, which every route into a
' binding passes through — so the bind delivers the held sentence and says so,
' the same way `commit` does above.
HeldForBind --> Idle : @delivered
HeldForBind --> Idle : @holdExpired / warnHoldExpired
HeldForBind --> Idle : 🔼 forward-left / dropHeld

@enduml
